Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["All Physics is Gauge Theory", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978638647735394*^9, 3.9786386508345337`*^9}, {
  3.978641316636702*^9, 3.978641319674756*^9}, {3.978737839482726*^9, 
  3.9787378449477777`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7c1aaaaf-5aaa-4d52-a80b-\
964e26b46f48"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A physics student usually first encounters the term \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in classical \
electrodynamics. However, the same notion pertains even in elementary physics \
in myriad ways. For an elementary example, consider measuring the altitude of \
an Earth satellite flying in a stable, circular, free-fall orbit. If we \
measure altitude with respect to mean sea level, the satellite seems to have \
a constant altitude, Earth\[CloseCurlyQuote]s oblateness aside. However, if \
we measure altitude with respect to the irregular surface of the Earth, the \
satellite\[CloseCurlyQuote]s altitude varies madly up and down. To naive \
observers, unaware of their poor choice of coordinate system, the satellite \
appears to suffer inexplicable forces pushing it up and down! However, these ",
 "apparent",
 " forces arise merely from the choice of ",
 StyleBox["gauge",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", that is, the definition of a measurement reference frame. Here, the term \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] fits entirely with its \
ordinary meaning, say the arbitrary origin of an altimeter or the width of a \
rail line, etc."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786386648875933`*^9, 3.978639147971436*^9}, {
  3.9786401089109507`*^9, 3.97864013021977*^9}, {3.978640191966693*^9, 
  3.978640516557682*^9}, {3.978641281651569*^9, 3.9786412836572237`*^9}, {
  3.978737855552356*^9, 3.9787379905163193`*^9}, {3.9787380221754427`*^9, 
  3.978738036037778*^9}, {3.9787889122095747`*^9, 3.978789038628954*^9}, {
  3.978789131640423*^9, 3.978789330099185*^9}, {3.978789377753706*^9, 
  3.978789388367732*^9}, {3.978789489346162*^9, 3.9787895396860113`*^9}, {
  3.9787897001908827`*^9, 
  3.978789714267542*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3b439049-7cf4-4a34-bc54-\
20d77b2ca349"],

Cell["\<\
A similar things happens in rotating reference frames. If we measure \
positions and momenta of free particles with respect to an inertial lab \
frame, we see no forces. If, however, we choose to measure from a rotating \
frame, we see centrifugal and Coriolis forces, arising merely from the choice \
of gauge, i.e., reference frame.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978639090934486*^9, 3.9786390959409924`*^9}, {
  3.9786391581020203`*^9, 3.9786392916461267`*^9}, {3.978639339607583*^9, 
  3.978639341057925*^9}, {3.978639843797641*^9, 3.978639883871458*^9}, {
  3.978640558948505*^9, 3.978640564055111*^9}, {3.978738055466886*^9, 
  3.978738056188883*^9}, {3.978789393960122*^9, 
  3.978789410670973*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"26cac6e5-0520-4bb4-8d59-\
23cca7409c14"],

Cell["\<\
Resolving these conundrums concisely requires gauge theory, totally pertinent \
to classical mechanics, but too heavy for introductory physics. That\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s why physics students don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t study gauge \
until they get into electrodynamics, where it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s some \
abstract, arbitrary field added to the vector potential, with no conceivable \
relationship to the ordinary meaning of the word. By that time, it\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s too late to go back and explain the apparent forces of \
elementary mechanics as arising merely from non-inertial gauge choices. Our \
poor physics students will carry multiple bags, all the way through general \
relativity (GR), until gauge appears again as more abstract wizardry in \
particle physics. They could have packed all their ideas into one piece of \
baggage with a concrete view of gauge as just a choice of reference frame.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978639302944932*^9, 3.978639559880187*^9}, {
   3.978639906097765*^9, 3.97863990678701*^9}, 3.978639968293231*^9, {
   3.9786400579528627`*^9, 3.9786400802416973`*^9}, {3.978640595978593*^9, 
   3.9786408470755568`*^9}, {3.978641348822749*^9, 3.97864137181462*^9}, {
   3.978738070996792*^9, 3.9787380861994247`*^9}, {3.978789438625586*^9, 
   3.978789478159536*^9}, {3.9787895499480867`*^9, 3.97878968026201*^9}, {
   3.978789744864238*^9, 3.978789876297686*^9}, {3.9787914565016108`*^9, 
   3.978791457765832*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6ceec6ac-1964-4e3a-8308-\
bc09bb1272c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["All forces, apparent and real, do, in fact, arise from choice of \
gauge",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". For the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]real\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] forces, we \
can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t choose a gauge that gets rid of them, as we could do \
in mechanics with inertial frames. But the ",
 StyleBox["symmetries",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of gauge choices drive forces, real and apparent, via Noether\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s theorem, which really should be the travel sticker on our \
baggage and the visa stamps in our passports as we journey through all of \
physics. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978640894250175*^9, 3.978641074879751*^9}, {
  3.978641407380624*^9, 3.9786414732143106`*^9}, {3.9786420394434547`*^9, 
  3.978642039792768*^9}, {3.9787381300235453`*^9, 3.978738138526342*^9}, {
  3.978789896455791*^9, 
  3.978789928750749*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"38b64028-6be8-42fb-8046-\
17cfbe0c10fc"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gauge Forces as Connections", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786365673927803`*^9, 3.9786365728569317`*^9}, {
  3.978637906305097*^9, 3.978637911784799*^9}, {3.978641629594967*^9, 
  3.978641632842622*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"de2e5ba2-e25c-4f93-bcd4-\
a727b1f176d3"],

Cell["\<\
We\[CloseCurlyQuote]re lucky. We\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve already studied \
covariant derivatives and connections in this series of notebooks, \
specifically in relativity, special and general. We\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve \
repeatedly seen that we can and should recast these ideas in terms of gauge \
theory. Now is the time, with the incandescent clarity that gauge is no more \
nor less than choice of reference frame in a generalized sense. We\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve seen that geometrical frame invariance, now geometrical \
gauge invariance, forces the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]discovery\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] of covariant derivative and connection. We\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve seen that such connections drive equations of motion, \
say for Schwarzschild orbits. We\[CloseCurlyQuote]re now positioned to \
explore the other forces of physics in the same terms.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978641572817196*^9, 3.978641680574541*^9}, {
  3.9786417137944403`*^9, 3.9786418997181177`*^9}, {3.978641933868432*^9, 
  3.978641951159326*^9}, {3.978738177896667*^9, 3.9787382112497663`*^9}, {
  3.978789968088002*^9, 
  3.9787900903971*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1a069641-6cc6-4768-99db-9d7dbb563bb2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Back to our physics students, with lighter baggage, encountering gauge \
again, ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for the first time, in classical electrodynamics. One realizes that the \
gradient of any differentiable scalar field \[CapitalLambda], called a gauge, \
can be added to the vector potential without altering the physics:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978636576303603*^9, 3.9786366785799294`*^9}, {
   3.978636723696795*^9, 3.978636870996152*^9}, {3.978636910194687*^9, 
   3.978636921670682*^9}, {3.9786370048263483`*^9, 3.9786370849609137`*^9}, 
   3.978637277938579*^9, {3.9786380563234453`*^9, 3.978638089888694*^9}, {
   3.978641485319695*^9, 3.9786415366166553`*^9}, {3.9786419540622797`*^9, 
   3.9786419851870832`*^9}, {3.978738229613509*^9, 3.978738232163897*^9}, {
   3.978738275893861*^9, 3.9787382803704367`*^9}, {3.978790103133443*^9, 
   3.978790176728155*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a613ee36-0c11-41f8-a3ac-\
7ed05a5d6d67"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox["A", "_"], 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["A", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637090481073*^9, 3.978637121098152*^9}, {
  3.9786372899247313`*^9, 3.978637455330873*^9}, {3.978637578634162*^9, 
  3.978637584593306*^9}, {3.978638122624658*^9, 
  3.978638130156509*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"32584ea5-15fb-48bb-b029-\
3d8673cac545"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In what sense is \[CapitalLambda] the choice of a reference frame? To \
resolve this conundrum, we have to see that electrodynamical gauge is also \
presented as ",
 StyleBox["phase invariance",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", a factor of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
    RowBox[{" ", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]}]], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"05497215-45aa-42e1-b0a6-22d1a630604b"],
 " that can be multiplied into a charged matter field (classical) or into a \
Dirac wave function (quantum) without altering the physics. Spoiler: choose \
phase in an abstract kind of reference frame; this is the ",
 StyleBox["primary",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " principle of electrodynamical gauge as a coordinate frame. Gradient added \
to vector potential is the necessary ",
 StyleBox["mechanism",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]induced \
transformation,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] required to uphold that principle. \
Here\[CloseCurlyQuote]s how that works."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978636576303603*^9, 3.9786366785799294`*^9}, {
  3.978636723696795*^9, 3.978636870996152*^9}, {3.978636910194687*^9, 
  3.978636921670682*^9}, {3.9786370048263483`*^9, 3.978637074091062*^9}, {
  3.9786374735329943`*^9, 3.97863749900111*^9}, {3.9786420889624434`*^9, 
  3.978642183847044*^9}, {3.978645450479156*^9, 3.978645504372199*^9}, {
  3.978738291981337*^9, 3.978738457947143*^9}, {3.978790183027944*^9, 
  3.9787902062151537`*^9}, {3.978790241679438*^9, 
  3.978790364497869*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f0ddc887-eb41-41eb-9130-\
415710d079c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Change a matter field \[Psi] by rotating its phase (gauge) by an arbitrary \
(but smoothly varying) amount, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8887eb8f-8e50-4c43-bc2b-5fa6ed172500"],
 ", at every point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "148377dc-a2d4-4c2d-ad37-7d9e8c50c6fa"],
 ", not changing the geometrical coordinates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "495da672-5450-4bd6-abfa-24210b59bf10"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637538672182*^9, 3.978637755565897*^9}, {
  3.978642236477104*^9, 3.978642246171332*^9}, {3.9787903747991543`*^9, 
  3.978790376943686*^9}, {3.978821792309321*^9, 
  3.978821810066669*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bbd91da1-9c66-4a41-b4ca-\
51cbc1f36766"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], "(", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
        SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}]], "\[Psi]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637538672182*^9, 3.97863778411996*^9}, {
  3.9786379712287197`*^9, 3.9786379796646557`*^9}, {3.978821290744693*^9, 
  3.978821330476513*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2699533f-e0e2-4931-b108-\
e52ba5a0a837"],

Cell["\<\
This is just like choosing a coordinate system with an arbitrary origin, \
locally, at each point, for the phase of the matter fields, without changing \
the spacetime geometry. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978642193583212*^9, 3.978642224078884*^9}, {
  3.9787384986624413`*^9, 3.978738566270625*^9}, {3.978790924023786*^9, 
  3.978790949934161*^9}, {3.978821303008254*^9, 3.9788213409196463`*^9}, {
  3.9788218407423058`*^9, 
  3.978821903531654*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2f9bbb0b-d116-44fa-86dd-\
f610d75178b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take the ordinary partial derivative, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dbe210c8-941f-4a8e-b180-8f7245a144d6"],
 ", of this new field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "cb83cb2a-980f-4291-9ce1-09b15724f99f"],
 ". The ordinary product rule spits out a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]garbage term\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CapitalLambda]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "140f5d75-b68e-465c-9c4e-2609eda551b2"],
 " varies with position:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637795314996*^9, 3.9786378832705383`*^9}, {
  3.978638180667034*^9, 3.9786381881906633`*^9}, {3.978642259537039*^9, 
  3.978642260939106*^9}, {3.978738583002688*^9, 3.978738586607667*^9}, {
  3.978790411450951*^9, 
  3.9787904159652767`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d709d7b9-a0b8-444c-a891-\
799112cdd05f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], "(", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
         SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}]], "  ", 
     RowBox[{"(", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
        RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "(", 
         SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"i", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
        RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "(", 
         SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}], "  ", ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
   "or", ",", " ", "abbreviating"}], TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
    OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "  ", 
    RowBox[{"(", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"i", "(", 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
       "\[Psi]"}]}], "  ", ")"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]}], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637887868793*^9, 3.9786378947514553`*^9}, {
  3.978637927473442*^9, 3.9786379497151003`*^9}, {3.978637985585307*^9, 
  3.9786380459954576`*^9}, {3.978638197487301*^9, 3.97863825659056*^9}, {
  3.978790463257308*^9, 3.978790502671747*^9}, {3.978790553765525*^9, 
  3.978790557365933*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"62e7a310-9def-4de0-b41b-\
525e0f7c85ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sound familiar? This is exactly what happened in relativity. The \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]garbage terms\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] drove our \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]discovery\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] of covariant \
derivative and connection coefficients. Here, the extra term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"i", "(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
    "\[Psi]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637887868793*^9, 3.9786378947514553`*^9}, {
   3.978637927473442*^9, 3.9786379497151003`*^9}, {3.978637985585307*^9, 
   3.9786380459954576`*^9}, {3.978638197487301*^9, 3.97863825659056*^9}},
  ExpressionUUID->"2d5d94d4-52a6-4301-98a1-27bff23628c1"],
 " ruins the rest of the physics. As before, we find that the ordinary \
derivative is not covariant: it doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t survive changes in \
phase coordinates."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978638433441883*^9, 3.978638454013837*^9}, {
  3.978638510142865*^9, 3.978638525977479*^9}, {3.978638574219385*^9, 
  3.9786385939606123`*^9}, {3.9786423189988194`*^9, 3.978642326146699*^9}, {
  3.978790523634274*^9, 3.97879052765222*^9}, {3.978790577036037*^9, 
  3.978790824183269*^9}, {3.978790987080504*^9, 3.978790987746471*^9}, {
  3.9788219390917053`*^9, 
  3.9788219693335457`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b44631bb-d396-4767-9ec4-\
dc3c65c2de71"],

Cell["\<\
With electrodynamics, compensating for the phase coordinate changes is \
easier. In GR, the gauge was the geometry itself, so compensating for \
coordinate change required 4D index manipulation. The electrodynamical \
connection is a one-index object because the electrodynamical gauge field is \
one-dimensional. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643141459524*^9, 3.9786431828556843`*^9}, {
  3.978738641173134*^9, 3.9787386532797832`*^9}, {3.9787908465552607`*^9, 
  3.978790856317902*^9}, {3.978791011986392*^9, 3.9787911783544617`*^9}, {
  3.978821976523123*^9, 
  3.978821990362543*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3414dda7-eeae-4408-b9c8-\
65d7bb7ac439"],

Cell["\<\
To clean up the electrodynamical gauge garbage, we need a correction term in \
our covariant derivative, just as we did with geometry and GR:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643216420027*^9, 3.978643271965823*^9}, {
  3.978791185639865*^9, 
  3.978791190604082*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c3bdd501-64cd-4593-9110-\
51b97f3a3483"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Congruent]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
     RowBox[{"-", "i"}]}], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643276164227*^9, 3.9786432889746*^9}, {
  3.978643322108322*^9, 3.978643337180196*^9}, {3.978643475279353*^9, 
  3.978643475281219*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4b3596e5-775e-4090-a055-\
8eaa17ef6d01"],

Cell["\<\
Yes, the connection is the vector potential, hence it drives forces! \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786433489592524`*^9, 3.978643399831469*^9}, {
  3.978643451260046*^9, 3.9786434570432673`*^9}, {3.978738674339534*^9, 
  3.9787386751608458`*^9}, {3.978791202722198*^9, 3.978791212226269*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"4bf37e51-2ef4-47e2-827e-789c2120b0a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the garbage terms to cancel out exactly, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cf9ccc92-131a-4340-9235-8ec665407f64"],
 " must transform as we learned in the first time in school, in Equation 1:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786433489592524`*^9, 3.978643399831469*^9}, {
  3.978643451260046*^9, 3.9786434570432673`*^9}, {3.978738674339534*^9, 
  3.9787386751608458`*^9}, {3.978791202722198*^9, 
  3.978791249452368*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a7c233ac-ac42-49e6-a9c8-\
3607a8c9035f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox["A", "_"], 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["A", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637090481073*^9, 3.978637121098152*^9}, {
  3.9786372899247313`*^9, 3.978637455330873*^9}, {3.978637578634162*^9, 
  3.978637584593306*^9}, {3.978638122624658*^9, 3.978638130156509*^9}, {
  3.9786434831358967`*^9, 
  3.978643484399239*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8246d647-b649-43c2-88f5-\
751f17de6404"],

Cell["Now we have ", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643488286076*^9, 3.9786434909815903`*^9}, {
  3.978791254151824*^9, 
  3.978791255677359*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"da41081c-7849-4055-973c-\
2f4774d27dcb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "\[Congruent]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786435032056303`*^9, 
  3.978643606837364*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"024e8a50-8217-4ff4-b17b-\
0b0e6867c4b7"],

Cell["and", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643593775935*^9, 
  3.978643594327322*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"32719714-8e0a-4b65-8a22-\
07f3d69ea5fc"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], 
    OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
      OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox["A", "_"], "\[Mu]"], 
      OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{"i", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
         "\[Psi]"}]}], ")"}]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox["A", "_"], "\[Mu]"], 
      OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"i", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
        "\[Psi]"}]}], ")"}]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"i", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["A", 
        RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
        RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
         RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "\[Psi]"}],
       ")"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}], 
    StyleBox["+",
     FontVariations->{"StrikeThrough"->True}], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "i", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
      "\[Psi]"}],
     FontVariations->{"StrikeThrough"->True}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "\[Psi]"}], 
    StyleBox["-",
     FontVariations->{"StrikeThrough"->True}], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "i", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
      "\[Psi]"}],
     FontVariations->{"StrikeThrough"->True}]}]}], TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "\[Psi]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "(", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      SubscriptBox["A", 
       RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "\[Psi]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]}], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786436192725773`*^9, 3.9786437727905197`*^9}, {
  3.978643806573044*^9, 3.978643946308076*^9}, {3.978644002327197*^9, 
  3.978644220022155*^9}, {3.978644291740561*^9, 3.9786443538434763`*^9}, {
  3.978644388511799*^9, 
  3.978644510127365*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a5eab264-474f-4226-a0ae-\
4d3f337c5c42"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "transforming covariantly with respect to the gauge choice ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b4f243b0-2c58-4140-977d-0486ffe6a72b"],
 ", exactly, if metaphorically to geometrical gauge in GR, covariant with its \
down index."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97864452629532*^9, 3.9786446238462*^9}, 
   3.978738689142243*^9, {3.978738724694315*^9, 3.978738784872237*^9}, {
   3.978791265368784*^9, 
   3.9787913061211567`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6e85698d-954f-469b-848a-\
601c91c29c9b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["We now see why it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a good idea, after all, to \
call the covariant derivative ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "covariant",
 StyleBox[". Such honors the metaphor everywhere without being exactly \
correct in GR, a fact we dismissed as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]historical\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in an earlier notebook.",
  FontSlant->"Italic"]
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978644642417985*^9, 3.978644753146748*^9}, {
  3.978645552948409*^9, 3.978645554732916*^9}, {3.978738701834901*^9, 
  3.978738704297278*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3eaa4828-6fd0-4989-bab6-\
6e2697261d66"],

Cell["\<\
We\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll write some new functions for the Relativity Toolkit to \
automate the calculation above, after just one last philosophical section, \
which bridges our old material for GR more deeply to the new material on \
gauges in general.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97864452629532*^9, 3.978644608759818*^9}, {
  3.9786447582836847`*^9, 3.978644803628751*^9}, {3.9786458816287622`*^9, 
  3.978645931893115*^9}, {3.978646349194942*^9, 3.978646350719452*^9}, {
  3.978791323640992*^9, 3.9787913558959093`*^9}, {3.978791495646101*^9, 
  3.9787915191520576`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ac12e704-4f80-48a5-b9da-\
4e11ea15a54f"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Covariant Derivatives, Revisited", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978358251530368*^9, 
  3.978358274502495*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7f6b77f4-b0fc-4a67-b903-\
969955fdadc1"],

Cell["\<\
In GR, we learned to take covariant derivatives of tensors that inhabit the \
tangent and cotangent tensor spaces of curved manifolds. The canonical \
example is the covariant derivative of a contravariant vector with respect to \
a basis of coordinate functions:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.978645997660583*^9}, {
  3.9787915036557417`*^9, 
  3.978791531715695*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4f010f30-76ff-4c9d-9e45-\
977a9562d116"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"example", "=", 
      RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
       RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"A", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Nu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
       "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Echo", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"TensorForm", "@@", "example"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"example", "\"\<\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978358547373548*^9, 3.978358772499927*^9}, {
  3.978359072474093*^9, 3.978359157811211*^9}, {3.9783592724273376`*^9, 
  3.978359272556822*^9}, {3.9783593063094587`*^9, 3.9783593921632147`*^9}, {
  3.978383680431888*^9, 3.978383735895418*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[14]:=",ExpressionUUID->"78497388-807e-47b1-a2f3-54ab4ce22561"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{"\<\"\"\>", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     TagBox[
      SubscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"A", 
        SuperscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], 
       RowBox[{";", "\[Nu]"}]],
      HoldForm], ")"}]}],
   "EchoLabel"], "  ", 
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SuperscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], 
     RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"A", 
       SuperscriptBox["", "\[Lambda]"]}], ")"}], " ", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "\[Lambda]"}], "\[Mu]"]}]}],
   HoldForm]}]], "Echo",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97887548557906*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ac6b598d-fdb1-401f-b028-09ddfc0dc10e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The connection coefficients \[CapitalGamma] account for the twisting and \
turning of basis vectors in the tangent spaces as the vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["A", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd3e6e84-9f68-483f-906e-506409ee1c30"],
 " is parallel-transported. In GR, this twisting and turning causes geodesics \
to converge or diverge"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.978646017572369*^9}, {
  3.978646073037752*^9, 3.978646096573864*^9}, {3.978791550457979*^9, 
  3.9787915716892157`*^9}, {3.978791607811911*^9, 
  3.978791645252721*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"37424616-b889-4f35-aa46-\
5f5a9d34df7f"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Geodesic deviation is indistinguishable from a force, \
but it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s not an apparent force: we can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
get rid of it by a gauge choice.",
 FontSlant->"Italic"]], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.978646017572369*^9}, {
  3.978646073037752*^9, 3.978646096573864*^9}, {3.978791550457979*^9, 
  3.9787915716892157`*^9}, {3.978791607811911*^9, 
  3.9787916688688183`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a0d3e19d-b357-44b9-be80-\
c725fc844522"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The derivative above transforms like a tensor, ensuring physics is ",
 StyleBox["locally Lorentz invariant",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". As noted in the introduction, this invariance is another application of \
Noether\[CloseCurlyQuote]s theorem. In GR, the conserved quantity arising \
from local Lorentz invariance is ",
 StyleBox["spin current",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", from symmetries of non-coordinate bases (see Appendix 1)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.97864602352232*^9}, {
  3.97864610862702*^9, 3.9786461676375427`*^9}, {3.978738857168982*^9, 
  3.978738864834247*^9}, {3.9787916844234667`*^9, 
  3.978791699695005*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9ad9e61c-cea4-41a0-a521-\
e599c7429130"],

Cell["\<\
In this notebook, we consider new spaces \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]attached\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] to points of the manifold like \
wallpaper\[LongDash]gauge fields representing electromagnetism and nuclear \
matter. These wallpaper spaces have their own differential geometries above \
and beyond the geometry of spacetime itself. In gravitation, gauge forces \
arise FROM the geometry. In other theories, gauge forces arise ON the \
geometry.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.9786460283023977`*^9}, {
  3.978646177642584*^9, 3.978646180024088*^9}, {3.978646219196919*^9, 
  3.978646221832672*^9}, {3.978738870146287*^9, 3.978738896485022*^9}, {
  3.9787917205922403`*^9, 
  3.978791794129325*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c95b6d04-962e-46a0-ac47-\
c90b44aaf33b"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["That\[CloseCurlyQuote]s one reason gravitation \
resists unification with the other forces of Nature, as explained more fully \
in the appendices.",
 FontSlant->"Italic"]], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97879180288661*^9, 
  3.978791833166924*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1d99b55f-d1a9-4711-bf92-\
f301849c4261"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "While it is fine for this notebook to envision gauge fields as \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]wallpaper,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] the rigorous \
mathematical machinery for this is that of ",
 StyleBox["fibre bundles",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (Appendix 2)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.97864603904847*^9}, {
  3.978646193604847*^9, 3.9786462612918663`*^9}, {3.978738915564204*^9, 
  3.978738919198637*^9}, {3.978791842137179*^9, 
  3.978791845890905*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"09d42c70-f660-41d6-91eb-\
a15c4faa3028"],

Cell["\<\
The goal of this notebook is to apply \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] to \
these wallpaper gauge fields, encoding transformation laws, invariants, and \
conserved quantities with the same rigor we applied to GR.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.978646049988058*^9}, {
  3.9786462670246687`*^9, 3.9786462749793463`*^9}, {3.978646305201108*^9, 
  3.978646320622986*^9}, {3.9787918538270893`*^9, 
  3.978791855215496*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e45636ff-3d1e-4a21-ac6b-\
fcb178545af0"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["A New CD", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978646468171488*^9, 
  3.978646472312533*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c8c2732a-482b-40dd-ad69-\
34c9e0e28e1c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This new overload of CD can compute Abelian gauge connections (sections of \
the principal bundle of Appendix 2). We\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll get to \
non-Abelian gauge connections like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"U", "(", "1", ")"}], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    RowBox[{"SU", "(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "4aa7d432-3705-4021-b822-69ca30d2c149"],
 " in future notebooks."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795270483778*^9, 3.978795277854451*^9}, {
  3.978795415257291*^9, 3.9787954500045643`*^9}, {3.978821069299505*^9, 
  3.978821143212737*^9}, {3.978821224035911*^9, 
  3.978821242453227*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9e34077f-ed2e-4587-87ba-\
5f5fa8adeb8f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gauge Covariant Derivative", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795468371107*^9, 
  3.978795488321023*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"94acbd51-3b62-4f9c-a4df-\
f9e4ff0aa53d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Inputs", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795503910904*^9, 
  3.9787955045961237`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ef67580c-d7d0-4644-b9c2-\
f49bb71314c8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["expr", "Input"],
 ": The field being differentiated, scalar or tensor"
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795528199066*^9, 
  3.978795548423512*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"85859702-2d3f-440a-9c1c-\
5c2d0a618c56"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["var", "Input"],
 ": the coordinate function, e.g., ",
 StyleBox["x[\[ScriptCapitalU][\[Mu]]]", "Input"],
 ", the differentiation variable"
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97879555492418*^9, 3.978795614319105*^9}, {
  3.97879576904465*^9, 
  3.978795773539029*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0ebc50f6-8428-4da3-99aa-\
009f03b3365b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["q", "Input"],
 ": the coupling constant or \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]charge\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]"
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795636372712*^9, 
  3.978795645409*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"77fc3235-4095-4d8d-96a1-e8b030336e52"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A", "Input"],
 ": the gauge-field connection symbol. \[CapitalGamma] is implicitly kept as \
the spacetime connection for all theories"
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9787956548435926`*^9, 
  3.9787956871354723`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"04154e59-9bc7-4076-b83d-\
31acad96ae89"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
    RowBox[{"expr_", ",", "var_", ",", "q_", ",", "A_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"gravitationalPart", ",", "gaugeCorrection", ",", "idx"}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", 
      RowBox[{
      "Calculate", " ", "the", " ", "coordinate", " ", "Covariant", " ", 
       "Derivative", " ", "via", " ", "existing", " ", "CD", " ", 
       RowBox[{"overloads", "."}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", 
      RowBox[{"Handle", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"+", " ", "Christoffels"}]}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"if", " ", "expr", " ", "is", " ", "a", " ", "tensor"}], 
        ")"}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"If", " ", "expr", " ", "is", " ", "a", " ", "scalar"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"just", " ", "return", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "."}]}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"gravitationalPart", "=", 
       RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
        RowBox[{"expr", ",", "var"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"(*", 
       RowBox[{
       "Extract", " ", "the", " ", "index", " ", "from", " ", "the", " ", 
        "differentiation", " ", 
        RowBox[{"variable", "."}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"(*", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"var", " ", "is", " ", "some", " ", 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
        RowBox[{"we", " ", "need", " ", "\[Mu]"}]}], "*)"}], 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"idx", "=", 
       RowBox[{"var", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      
      RowBox[{"(*", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Construct", " ", "the", " ", "Gauge", " ", "Correction"}], ",",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{"e", ".", "g", "."}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "i"}], " ", "q", " ", 
         SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"], " ", "*", " ", "expr"}]}], "*)"}], 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"(*", 
       RowBox[{"Note", ":", " ", 
        RowBox[{"This", " ", "A", " ", "has", " ", "a", " ", "DOWN", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", "Covariant", ")"}], " ", "index", " ", "matching", " ", 
         "the", " ", "derivative"}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"gaugeCorrection", "=", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], "*", "q", "*", 
        RowBox[{"A", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "idx", "]"}], "]"}], "*", 
        "expr"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"(*", "Combine", "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"gravitationalPart", "+", "gaugeCorrection"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978646744556492*^9, 3.978646885622224*^9}, 
   3.978724934490802*^9, {3.978795290664665*^9, 3.9787954073020678`*^9}, 
   3.9787954931896*^9, {3.9787956971832857`*^9, 3.978795753281424*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[15]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3de2c0a4-4890-4dcd-8310-578ba58e364c"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Electrodynamics Demos", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978700005346057*^9, 3.9787000089781*^9}, {
   3.9787963301955833`*^9, 3.9787963317746277`*^9}, 3.9788004955698223`*^9, 
   3.978821216010556*^9},ExpressionUUID->"2c02b0be-4c78-4b2a-a1b3-\
4a70d6e26bf1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Covariance of the Covariant Derivative", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823576434066*^9, 3.978823591975399*^9}, {
  3.9788236656529293`*^9, 3.978823667365944*^9}, {3.9788607083047037`*^9, 
  3.978860710361669*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"26cab6eb-fabb-4147-9085-\
2e72df92e4fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Forces as Gauge Connections,\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] above, we subjected the following expression to a 1D \
(Abelian) gauge transformation \[LineSeparator]in a manual calculation, now \
including a specific, constant charge, ",
 StyleBox["q",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978820844121111*^9, 3.97882093662414*^9}, {
  3.978821545485203*^9, 3.978821615299986*^9}, {3.978822440304517*^9, 
  3.978822451496654*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"db673d5e-f1b1-4938-a6c8-\
a394f4250e7e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"(", 
  RowBox[{"cde", "=", 
   RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "q", ",", 
     "A"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978646926181177*^9, 3.978646943909356*^9}, {
   3.97864698544555*^9, 3.97864700656507*^9}, 3.97880072568736*^9, {
   3.978818102147591*^9, 3.978818102997529*^9}, {3.978820978904854*^9, 
   3.978820983247849*^9}, 3.978821610399053*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[18]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e8d9c61f-9eb0-4945-ad72-568d5242b5c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], " ", "q", " ", "\[Psi]", " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"A", 
     SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
  SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
   RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9788754856206923`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[18]=",ExpressionUUID->"1e373bc9-9177-4023-8982-ba1fb9326e88"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s automate that calculation. Starting with the gauge \
transformations\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978820911086568*^9, 3.978820944821334*^9}, {
  3.978822642442547*^9, 
  3.9788226595359287`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bfcbf30b-9a8f-4a6b-b946-\
5c4170da5fd0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{
       "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "\[Psi]", "    ", "and", "    ", 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox["A", "_"], 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
       SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}], " "}]}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637538672182*^9, 3.97863778411996*^9}, {
   3.9786379712287197`*^9, 3.9786379796646557`*^9}, {3.978821290744693*^9, 
   3.978821330476513*^9}, {3.978822473550243*^9, 3.978822480144888*^9}, {
   3.978822548622191*^9, 3.978822571486229*^9}, 3.978822679099642*^9, {
   3.978822842709276*^9, 
   3.978822852781521*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bcfea902-d337-4bda-b9ad-\
532a59a7d4c0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gaugeTransforms", "=", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "->", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[ImaginaryI]", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], "\[Psi]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]_", "]"}], "]"}], ":>", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"A", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"Partials", "[", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"x", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
       "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978821001702631*^9, 3.978821044361678*^9}, {
   3.978821351660639*^9, 3.9788214177368813`*^9}, {3.978821448541462*^9, 
   3.97882146930516*^9}, {3.978821639276532*^9, 3.978821662429945*^9}, {
   3.978822191621005*^9, 3.9788221929215384`*^9}, 3.978822231151826*^9, {
   3.978823334810932*^9, 3.978823335460462*^9}, 3.978825160269917*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[19]:=",ExpressionUUID->"727a63da-aa90-45dd-adc5-0ffe24da003b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "q", " ", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], " ", 
     "\[Psi]"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"A", 
     SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]_"]}], "\[RuleDelayed]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], "+", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
      RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.978875485625252*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[19]=",ExpressionUUID->"0326258a-77c4-471c-9968-db138e338854"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["prove that the covariant derivative", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978822728959449*^9, 3.978822748830817*^9}, {
  3.978822863916007*^9, 
  3.978822865933402*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"50c162a4-95b1-4c2d-9f84-\
dcfd4b83f679"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "\[Congruent]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786435032056303`*^9, 3.978643606837364*^9}, {
  3.978822966772187*^9, 
  3.97882296838054*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7eeea367-8db9-4bb8-83e0-\
0b1addaa1107"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData["cde"], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97882295539398*^9, 3.9788229747395887`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[20]:=",ExpressionUUID->"74aa2717-20d8-4b85-8c00-75156a11cebb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], " ", "q", " ", "\[Psi]", " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"A", 
     SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
  SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
   RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.978875485634665*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[20]=",ExpressionUUID->"904fc3b2-0c6c-46a7-87c7-d63a6862bffd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["transforms exactly the same way as \[Psi]", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978822755950194*^9, 3.9788227570842133`*^9}, {
  3.978822823242772*^9, 
  3.978822836885271*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"73ecf68b-5a23-4059-bef3-\
42897e2d257f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], 
    OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{
      "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], 
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786436192725773`*^9, 3.9786437727905197`*^9}, {
  3.978643806573044*^9, 3.978643946308076*^9}, {3.978644002327197*^9, 
  3.978644220022155*^9}, {3.978644291740561*^9, 3.9786443538434763`*^9}, {
  3.978644388511799*^9, 3.978644510127365*^9}, {3.978822775213642*^9, 
  3.978822798371068*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"19bf54b0-a557-49f3-bd18-\
9d2c3b9dbd1d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We just need one rule for the charge constant. Everything else is already \
in the toolkit\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 StyleBox["differentiationRules", "Input"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978822882032498*^9, 3.9788229273306627`*^9}, {
  3.978823009564211*^9, 
  3.978823010008813*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"63449289-cd0b-41a0-9449-\
cf2944636b07"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"constantRules", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Partials", "[", 
     RowBox[{"q", ",", 
      RowBox[{"x", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]_", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ",
     ":>", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788220405709257`*^9, 3.9788220914844437`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[21]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3f172635-6ee5-4a70-8a61-eb7d220f695e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["q", 
    RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]_"}]], "\[RuleDelayed]", "0"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.978875485637438*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[21]=",ExpressionUUID->"c700f2b3-ed8f-40a8-aa9a-dd2695804ede"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"transformedCde", "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"cde", " ", "/.", " ", "gaugeTransforms"}], " ", "//.", " ", 
      "differentiationRules"}], "/.", "constantRules"}], "//", "Expand"}], "//",
    "Simplify"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978822102593217*^9, 3.978822112777665*^9}, {
   3.9788222776342163`*^9, 3.9788222792555733`*^9}, {3.9788223692243032`*^9, 
   3.97882240547611*^9}, 3.978823022815748*^9, {3.978823148683112*^9, 
   3.97882316041686*^9}, {3.978823349405294*^9, 3.9788233500015306`*^9}, {
   3.978858170112883*^9, 3.97885818491053*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[22]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b0ec1902-d500-41fa-8f61-43ad9f584e95"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
   RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "q", " ", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], " ", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], " ", "q", " ", "\[Psi]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"A", 
       SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
     RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}], ")"}]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.978875485651066*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[22]=",ExpressionUUID->"1ba801f6-6f06-4195-a7b1-cec48b537f4c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"transformedCde", "===", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[ImaginaryI]", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], "cde"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823164654051*^9, 3.97882321873451*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[23]:=",ExpressionUUID->"799324fc-d50c-48e5-bdb5-66f0d5e3b2d1"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.97887548565317*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[23]=",ExpressionUUID->"46841517-6df6-4ace-a953-c910da93d860"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["QED\[NonBreakingSpace]\[FilledSquare]", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823232236299*^9, 
  3.978823321181185*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ad7c97ba-d85c-4acc-97c1-\
ef3e695d61dd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Invariance of the Field-Strength Tensor", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823650174912*^9, 3.9788236824567013`*^9}, {
  3.978823896569426*^9, 
  3.978823898592578*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"13a5b2c2-e39a-477b-935b-\
59de3331ef7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The field-strength tensor, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["F", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Nu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a78e8c4-fc08-4a8e-92f9-ce12438ddaad"],
 ", aka Faraday, is defined as follows"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978824061078446*^9, 
  3.978824098440377*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8f3ecd75-5900-473e-ad73-\
516a0e7c21fe"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"F", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "]"}]}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Partials", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Nu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"Partials", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Nu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823709235116*^9, 3.9788237415322437`*^9}, {
  3.978824044627816*^9, 3.978824051061049*^9}, {3.978824190166666*^9, 
  3.9788241975067244`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[24]:=",ExpressionUUID->"097fd1ac-3cb5-4783-9706-68f9adb7f946"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"-", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], 
     RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]], ")"}]}], "+", 
  SubscriptBox[
   RowBox[{"A", 
    SubscriptBox["", "\[Nu]"]}], 
   RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.978875485655203*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[24]=",ExpressionUUID->"41919462-89d7-4303-a827-ef3f215fb2cb"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "usually presented as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Nu]"}]]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Nu]"], 
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0b7b22c-4b20-45e1-9116-61a69b483886"],
 " to make the indices line up, but our notation checks out."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978824215276784*^9, 
  3.978824267149712*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"686c6855-f4f0-4413-b371-\
5d14d6d91172"],

Cell["Now, subject it to the gauge transform:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788242749841127`*^9, 
  3.9788242924403057`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bf1fd84a-386a-4f24-b9a9-\
614cbd977b06"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"F", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "]"}], "/.", " ", 
  "gaugeTransforms"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:=",ExpressionUUID->"41f7d312-8c5c-4141-b7fe-24720dee4831"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"A", 
       SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], "+", 
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
       RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}], ")"}], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]]}], "+", 
  SubscriptBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Nu]"]}], "+", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
      RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]]}], ")"}], 
   RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9788754856601963`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[25]=",ExpressionUUID->"d568e2fd-3c12-4c82-884b-bae10f2659d8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "See that it doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t change by invoking the toolkit\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 StyleBox["ExpandDerivatives", "Input"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978824312009261*^9, 
  3.978824333879499*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"91ab7ee2-27ab-479b-9a7a-\
fcd44e4d6e2e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"F", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "]"}], "/.", " ", "gaugeTransforms"}], 
  " ", "//", " ", "ExpandDerivatives", " "}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823798335211*^9, 3.9788238192571917`*^9}, 
   3.978823885830079*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[26]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3e9266b1-4af3-4050-81a7-4a26104483a3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"-", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], 
     RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]], ")"}]}], "+", 
  SubscriptBox[
   RowBox[{"A", 
    SubscriptBox["", "\[Nu]"]}], 
   RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.978875485669855*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[26]=",ExpressionUUID->"b96c7799-7675-4f56-9a09-48e43b47202a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["QED\[NonBreakingSpace]\[FilledSquare]", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823232236299*^9, 
  3.978823321181185*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e0e8b96a-c1ba-4281-b112-\
8fab9afc7dd6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Note: Charge Conservation as a Consequence", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978824417541904*^9, 
  3.978824442338882*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2096586f-c18f-4206-96a3-\
083d7a520f51"],

Cell["\<\
By proving that the covariant derivative transforms just by a phase factor, \
we proved that physical laws built from these derivatives remain invariant \
(unchanged) under gauge transformations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.978824498584906*^9}, {
  3.978824793647162*^9, 
  3.978824804138522*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3b492fc4-9746-4c7b-bbe3-\
24412597a077"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the Lagrangian, phase factors in terms like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], 
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f39fa4f-ea97-4bac-9f03-d117e7518abe"],
 " cancel (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{
     "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], 
    "*", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "i"}], "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      "\[CapitalLambda]"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2021a6dd-cac1-47c4-baf3-2ac2eaafb0a8"],
 "), showing our theory has a continuous-in-\[CapitalLambda] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"U", 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2116f244-5f11-4b19-8032-0415b94708e9"],
 " symmetry (invariance)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.978824642047434*^9}, {
  3.978824843512475*^9, 
  3.978824866239888*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"10affd0a-26b4-4de8-9414-\
7f0877557db1"],

Cell["\<\
According to Noether\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Theorem, every continuous symmetry \
implies a conservation law.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 
  3.978824657601129*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"68c0c2a0-1b5d-45cf-9efe-\
d9ad1c9d79e6"],

Cell["time-translation symmetry \[DoubleLongRightArrow] conservation of \
energy", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.978824660443276*^9}, {
  3.9788246931582336`*^9, 
  3.9788247246785107`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1818a92a-ac0c-4215-97aa-\
778ebbffd45b"],

Cell["spatial translation symmetry \[DoubleLongRightArrow] conservation of \
momentum", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.9788246636498423`*^9}, {
  3.978824697325098*^9, 3.978824697877668*^9}, {3.9788247314028273`*^9, 
  3.9788247475931168`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6d3a0f86-db22-4d7c-a644-\
f66a735c0cce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"U", 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "0794a4d9-60d2-4afd-92c2-25f9c9468256"],
 " phase symmetry \[DoubleLongRightArrow] conservation of electric charge"
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.97882470049264*^9}, {
  3.9788247519693537`*^9, 
  3.978824763905596*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"24030461-d0a4-4602-925d-\
c4b1213ef2fb"],

Cell["\<\
Thus, the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge correction\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
geometry is the direct mathematical reason that electric charge is conserved.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.9788246781707687`*^9}, {
  3.9788248817520447`*^9, 
  3.9788249338572903`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ce728114-899c-41d0-a246-\
85360f6e9cc8"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Weinberg-Salam Mixed-Gauge Demo", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9787963383682137`*^9, 3.97879634402703*^9}, {
  3.9788180610060997`*^9, 3.978818067081018*^9}, {3.978825674286153*^9, 
  3.978825699794757*^9}, {3.9788558949345093`*^9, 
  3.978855894989732*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8ac3c528-684d-4beb-ab6b-\
4d1874e0ecab"],

Cell["Charged Vector Boson Covariance (U (1) Sector)", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978825680281598*^9, 
  3.97882568358232*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ed309d12-628c-4101-a914-\
cbf434fe8e88"],

Cell["We proceed just as above", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788249780669603`*^9, 
  3.978824986166164*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f028ebea-692c-482c-9daa-\
62ea02d7489e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"wsd", "=", 
    RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"W", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "gW", ",",
       "Z"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "//", "TensorForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978646926181177*^9, 3.978646944946294*^9}, {
   3.9786470457728977`*^9, 3.978647062184148*^9}, {3.9788243635656977`*^9, 
   3.978824398969141*^9}, 3.978824990560746*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[27]:=",ExpressionUUID->"67be8f28-c827-4885-9074-9540eca97413"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"W", 
     SuperscriptBox["", "\[Alpha]"]}], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]], "-", 
